WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.469
-[ Heavy sigh ]
Hi, everyone.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.304
It's Jimmy Fallon.
Welcome to another edition

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.873
of "The Tonight Show
At Home Edition."

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:09.376
Today is Friday

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:12.545
and I know every day kind of
feels the same, a little bit,

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:16.215
but, today kind of feels
like a Friday again.

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:18.984
First time in a long time,
I think, you know?

00:00:18.984 --> 00:00:23.289
And it's been a week.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:26.059
It's been, you know,
a lot of time, but,

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.294
I have no plan
for the weekend.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.363
Normally, I'm...

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.364
pumpin' it up.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.464
"Let's go to the beach.

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:33.733
Let's go to the play.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.334
We'll do something,
then we'll have a play date!

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.803
We'll do this;
we'll dah dah."

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.704
Nothing.
I got nothing for the kids.

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:40.739
So the kids have that
to look forward to --

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:43.309
absolutely [ Laughing ]
nothing this weekend.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.378
We're staying at home
like we're supposed to do

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.780
and it's kind of fun,
in a weird way.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.916
It's freeing.
I'm actually, uh,

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:54.219
happy to be here,
lucky to be here and safe and...

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:56.656
that's what I'm gonna do.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.992
And I'm gonna try not to,
you know,

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:03.896
overthink everything and take
every day one day at a time.

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:05.331
I thank you all
for watching.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.500
I thank NBC for airing this.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.170
YouTube, for airing it
on YouTube as well,

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.706
for the people that don't
have cable or a TV.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:14.707
They can watch our shows.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.476
Thank you for donating.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.578
State Farm.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.813
Our good neighbors
at State Farm.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:22.048
Where is that?

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.248
There it is.

00:01:23.248 --> 00:01:25.185
Winnie wrote this out.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.485
Kind of rushed it today, I feel.

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.387
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:32.926
-Redcross.org/statefarm.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.560
State Farm said they'd match

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.197
up to $200,000 this week
in donations.

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.132
That's $400,000.

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:42.601
We're very close
to reaching $200,000,

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:43.869
I'm very happy to say.

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:46.172
[ Clapping] I love you guys.
That's awesome.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:50.342
So, that means $400,000
have been donated to Red Cross,

00:01:50.342 --> 00:01:51.711
thanks to you guys.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.380
They matched --
They matched your donation.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.883
Thank you to our neighbors
at State Farm

00:01:56.883 --> 00:02:01.787
and our friends at Red Cross
are so, so thankful and happy.

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.289
We talked to them today
and they wanted

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:06.459
to let everyone know to please
give blood, if you can.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.861
I'm not hearing Winnie.

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:11.230
-Why are you doing that?

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.498
-I thought that was Gary.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.367
I was like, "Wait.
Gary can open the door?"

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.002
-No.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.037
-Who is that?
-I want inclusion!

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.239
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.773
Guys, I thought
you were already upstairs.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.141
Hi. Nice to see ya.
-Hi.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:23.509
-Oh.
-Wait. Give it to me.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:24.977
-Oh.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.580
Hi, guys.
-Hi.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.850
-Anyways, if you can --

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:31.984
I'll close the door.
Don't worry.

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:33.386
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:34.753 --> 00:02:36.956
[ Running footsteps ]

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.558
-Hey.
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.159
-I was try-- Sure.
[ Piano playing ]

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.293
-She got the note about...

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:42.362
[ Laughs ]

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.130
-[ Heavy sigh ]
-...putting her coat on.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.531
-[ Laughing ] It was
so quiet for a second.

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:47.767
It was so quiet for a second.
[ Sigh ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.803
Anyways, if you can give blood,
please give blood.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:54.373
They need blood donations,
please.

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:56.341
And my guest tonight,

00:02:56.341 --> 00:02:58.144
Miley Cyrus, [ Clap ]

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.845
the coolest kid in school,
has been doing a show

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:03.449
on Instagram Live for the past
three weeks, a talk show.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.986
So she now knows what it's like
to be a talk show host

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.521
and so, I wanna talk
to her about that.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:11.557
Also her foundation is
happyhippies.org.

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:12.992
Oh, Winnie, come on.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.360
This is --
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.262
-I mean, come on.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:19.599
Anyways, that's supposed
to say happyhippies.org.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:22.501
They're doing amazing stuff
for homeless youth,

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:27.573
but they're switching up their
initiative for this pandemic.

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:30.176
You'll see what she has to say.
She's great.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:34.646
Also, we have
Rachel Brosnahan, who,

00:03:34.646 --> 00:03:39.652
covenanthouse.org
is her charity.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.488
Please give to that.
We're talking to Rachel,

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.789
"The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel."

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:45.925
And then, we have music
from Lewis Capaldi!

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.193
[ Clapping ] My man!

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:50.662
[ Scat singing ]

00:03:50.662 --> 00:03:52.265
I love that song so much.

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:54.500
♪ I need somebody to heal ♪

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.701
♪ Somebody to love ♪

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:59.272
[ Mumbling lyrics ]

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.940
♪ Now the day bleeds ♪

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.241
♪ Into nightfall ♪

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:03.543
Thank you, Frannie.

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.677
Anyways,
he's on the show tonight,

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.011
performing a song
from that album.

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:07.246
I love Lewis Capaldi.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:08.347
Guys, let's start the show.

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:09.949
It's Friday,
"Tonight Show."

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.984
Let's do a mono,
monologue, right now.

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:15.888
♪♪

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:16.956
Alright, welcome

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.157
to "The Tonight Show
At Home Edition."

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:19.725
Well, guys, it is Friday, so,

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:22.228
congrats on getting through
another workweek on Zoom

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.965
without your boss noticing
you're drunk or stoned.

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:28.000
Listen to this -- There's
a petition gaining momentum

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.502
to name Dr. Fauci

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:33.072
People magazine's
Sexiest Man Alive.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.440
You know these are crazy times

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.075
when the Sexiest Man Alive vote
is gonna come down to

00:04:37.075 --> 00:04:40.712
Dr. Fauci and Joe Exotic.
♪♪

00:04:40.712 --> 00:04:42.181
If Dr. Fauci doesn't win,

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.716
he should at least get
People magazine's

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:46.552
Sexiest Man Trying
to Keep You Alive.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:47.987
♪♪

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.521
That's good.

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:51.156
CNN's Chris Cuomo said

00:04:51.156 --> 00:04:54.827
he's lost 13 pounds in 3 days
due to coronavirus.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:55.895
So, it's official --

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.963
I definitely don't have
coronavirus.

00:04:57.963 --> 00:05:01.233
♪♪

00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:03.135
My man boobs looking weird
-[ Laughing ]

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:05.138
-in this light?

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.306
I'll just do this like this.

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:11.510
I saw that more than 12,000
people just applied

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.612
to be a NASA astronaut.

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:16.749
Yep. Everyone spent two weeks
with their family and thought,

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.250
"I gotta get out to space."

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:21.520
♪♪

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.755
Sir Andrew Lloyd Webber

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.891
is now streaming Broadway
shows online for free.

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.093
My wife will probably
enjoy that more

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:29.362
than me singing "Phantom" songs

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:32.331
with a surgical mask
covering half my face.

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:34.967
♪ Slowly ♪

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:40.205
[ Singing indistinctly ]

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:43.542
♪ I am in a sewer ♪

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:47.780
♪ Trying to find love ♪

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.715
Never saw "Phantom."

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:51.150
I can only assume
that's what it was, right?

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.819
He live in a sewer?
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:55.254
-He has a mask or something.
♪♪

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.755
I get it.

00:05:56.755 --> 00:05:59.391
People love -- The heart wants
what the heart wants, you know?

00:05:59.391 --> 00:06:01.928
♪♪

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:04.130
I saw Tom Brady
is moving his family

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.932
into Derek Jeter's
mansion in Tampa.

00:06:06.932 --> 00:06:08.367
Though it's not
a done deal, yet.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:11.671
First, Jeter smartly wants
to run a credit check on Brady

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:14.073
[ Laughter ] and get first
and last month's rent up-front.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.374
Very smart.

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:16.542
You never know, man.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.578
[ Laughs ]

00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:20.512
Dwayne Johnson posted
a video on Instagram

00:06:20.512 --> 00:06:21.680
about washing your hands,

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.050
where he's shirtless,
in just a towel,

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:26.485
and rapping a song from "Moana."

00:06:26.485 --> 00:06:28.253
Yeah. When Dwayne
does that, it's fun,

00:06:28.253 --> 00:06:29.322
but when I do that, it's

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.090
"Dad, you're ruining
homeschool."

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:34.026
♪♪

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.461
And, finally,
according to scientists,

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:39.999
mice can actually make facial
expressions based on their mood.

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:42.134
Americans heard that
and were like, "That's great.

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:44.470
Any word on the cure
for coronavirus?"

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:47.940
♪♪

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.875
Mice can --

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:51.343
That's our monologue
for tonight.

00:06:51.343 --> 00:06:54.179
Hey, I think it's time
for "Thank You Notes"!

00:06:54.179 --> 00:06:55.347
Girls, get down here!

00:06:55.347 --> 00:06:56.348
Help out Daddy!

00:06:56.348 --> 00:06:58.684
[ Funk sting plays ]

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.253
-Hey, guys.
Today's Friday and,

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.854
even though we're quarantined,
it's still a day

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:04.056
where I check my inbox;
return some emails;

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:06.392
and, of course, I send out
thank-you notes.

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:07.793
[ Laughing ]
Well, I was wondering

00:07:07.793 --> 00:07:09.896
if I could write out my weekly
thank-you notes right now.

00:07:09.896 --> 00:07:15.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.202
Frannie, can I get some
thank-you note writing

00:07:17.202 --> 00:07:18.270
music, please?

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.305
[ Tender theme plays ]

00:07:20.305 --> 00:07:21.574
That's good; that's good.

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.208
That's good.

00:07:23.208 --> 00:07:25.444
Thank you, wearing a hat,

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:27.479
for being the new
taking a shower.

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:30.682
[ Whispering ] Go.
Good job.

00:07:30.682 --> 00:07:32.150
Thank you, home gyms,

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:34.086
for making me realize
that every time I said,

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:37.323
"If I only had more free time,"
I was just lying to myself.

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:38.424
♪♪

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:43.429
♪♪

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:45.731
Thank you,
making homemade pizza.

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:47.700
Yes, it takes much longer
than delivery

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.202
and involves way more effort,
but, in the end,

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:51.437
it tastes terrible.

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:56.142
♪♪

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:57.977
-Are you ready?
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:57.977 --> 00:07:59.144
Winnie, perfect.

00:07:59.144 --> 00:08:00.846
♪♪

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:02.982
-Thank you,
tracking a package,

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.283
for being
the closest thing I have

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:06.018
to watching sports right now.

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:07.286
"Oh.

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:08.721
Oh, it's in Iowa!

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:11.924
The package made it
to Iowa, guys!" Okay.

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:15.427
♪♪

00:08:15.427 --> 00:08:19.298
Thank you, the phrase
"How you holdin' up?"

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:21.466
for being the polite way
of asking someone,

00:08:21.466 --> 00:08:23.769
"So, are you also
on the brink of insanity?"

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:25.604
-[ Chuckle ]
-[ Chuckle ]

00:08:25.604 --> 00:08:26.872
-Hm?
-Yeah.

00:08:26.872 --> 00:08:29.007
That's perfect.
Don't touch.

00:08:29.007 --> 00:08:30.209
Thank you, KFC,

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:34.146
for giving away a million
pieces of fried chicken.

00:08:34.146 --> 00:08:38.083
Just maybe don't tell people
it's Finger Lickin' Good.

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:40.920
It's Rubber Glovin'
Finger Licking Good.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.857
♪♪

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:46.758
Thank you, weather app,

00:08:46.758 --> 00:08:48.661
for reminding me
that there's weather.

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:50.796
♪♪

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:51.998
Alright. Good.

00:08:51.998 --> 00:08:53.699
Last one.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:56.434
Thank you,
yoga classes over Zoom,

00:08:56.434 --> 00:08:57.670
for occasionally becoming

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.605
just 16 close-ups of butts.

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:00.605
♪♪

00:09:00.605 --> 00:09:02.041
What do you think
of those jokes?

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:04.042
That or this one?

00:09:04.042 --> 00:09:05.744
[ Booing ]

00:09:05.744 --> 00:09:07.412
-[ Laughing ]
-Guys, we'll be right back

00:09:07.412 --> 00:09:09.281
with more "Tonight Show."
We have [ Laughing ] Miley Cyrus

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:12.584
on the show
and we have Rachel Brosnahan.

00:09:12.584 --> 00:09:13.686
-I didn't see this one.
-And Lewis Capaldi.

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:15.688
Thank you, Winnie.
You didn't see that one?

00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:16.989
It's funny. Good job, Winnie.

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:18.190
Good job, Frannie.
We'll be right back, everybody.

